1
00:00:00,620 --> 00:00:02,120
Go!

2
00:00:02,710 --> 00:00:04,000
Kickoff!

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,130
You got this!

4
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:12,180
We have one strength
and one strength only.

5
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:14,180
An advantage in numbers!

6
00:00:14,180 --> 00:00:15,010
SHIN TENMA RYOHEI JUZO
KITO

7
00:00:15,010 --> 00:00:18,430
If we keep passing to whoever's open...

8
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:19,890
There it is!

9
00:00:20,350 --> 00:00:21,350
O-Ogami!

10
00:00:24,730 --> 00:00:25,480
Huh?

11
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:26,940
He was on the opposite side!

12
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:28,400
He's fast!

13
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:35,030
Let's start things off
with a little hello, shall we?

14
00:00:35,490 --> 00:00:37,080
He's shooting already?

15
00:00:42,620 --> 00:00:43,500
Huh?

16
00:00:46,380 --> 00:00:47,340
No way!

17
00:00:47,340 --> 00:00:48,500
He knocked the goal over!

18
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:58,050
Boss, be careful!
Don't blow your cover with a kick!

19
00:00:58,050 --> 00:00:59,060
Like I care.

20
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:01,060
I'll worry about excuses...

21
00:01:01,390 --> 00:01:04,310
after I wipe that smug look off his face!

22
00:01:13,490 --> 00:01:14,650
Out of bounds!

23
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:16,820
Kick-in for the home ec team!

24
00:01:19,030 --> 00:01:20,240
Was that for real?

25
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:22,000
That was actually kinda crazy!

26
00:01:23,040 --> 00:01:25,330
That was way beyond "kinda"!

27
00:01:25,330 --> 00:01:26,750
Tenma's...

28
00:01:27,630 --> 00:01:31,090
kicking power is totally pro-level, but...

29
00:01:32,420 --> 00:01:33,510
Not bad.

30
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:35,970
Well, I can kick things at least.

31
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:39,010
I've never lost a game of 
Kick the Can for distance.

32
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:12,980
HOW ABOUT A "THANK YOU"?
SATURDAY, MAY 16th

33
00:03:14,980 --> 00:03:17,150
Ooh, look at Oga go!

34
00:03:17,150 --> 00:03:21,610
Did he forget that whole "living quietly
and staying under the radar" thing?

35
00:03:21,610 --> 00:03:23,240
Wow, Ogami's incredible!

36
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:25,030
That was amazing!

37
00:03:25,030 --> 00:03:27,540
Wait, could this actually 
turn into a real match?

38
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:28,710
Huh? Wait...

39
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,040
Oh, I'll take the kick-in.

40
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:32,330
Thanks.

41
00:03:34,170 --> 00:03:35,460
What's wrong, Shin?

42
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:39,220
Kohazame?

43
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:41,720
D-Dude, where's your pacifier?

44
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:43,340
I-I don't... see it.

45
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:44,930
Huh? Sea lion?

46
00:03:44,930 --> 00:03:47,390
Wait, was it when you tried
to block that shot?

47
00:03:47,390 --> 00:03:49,230
Los... Blancos.

48
00:03:49,230 --> 00:03:52,600
Without his pacifier, this guy turns
into a useless bundle of stage fright.

49
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:53,230
What?

50
00:03:53,480 --> 00:03:54,900
Honestly, before anything else...

51
00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:57,820
I was wondering why he was
 always sucking on that thing.

52
00:03:57,820 --> 00:03:59,030
Right?

53
00:03:59,440 --> 00:04:00,360
Ah...

54
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:03,280
Must've knocked it loose
when it grazed him.

55
00:04:03,570 --> 00:04:05,280
Do you have a spare?

56
00:04:07,620 --> 00:04:10,750
Um, he says there's one
in his bag in the classroom!

57
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:12,080
I'll go get it!

58
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,460
I'll go, too!

59
00:04:13,460 --> 00:04:14,830
Thank you!

60
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:16,500
Fine.

61
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:18,210
Just stand here for now.

62
00:04:18,210 --> 00:04:20,050
Maybe you'll at least be in their way.

63
00:04:20,050 --> 00:04:24,050
Our advantage is gone!
Now it's just a normal 2v2!

64
00:04:24,050 --> 00:04:24,970
Hey!

65
00:04:24,970 --> 00:04:27,560
Can we get this game going again already?

66
00:04:30,140 --> 00:04:33,100
Noren, he wants you to be 
his lap pillow and pat his head?

67
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:34,520
That's his dream?

68
00:04:34,850 --> 00:04:36,110
That's what he said.

69
00:04:36,110 --> 00:04:37,900
Everything about him is over the top!

70
00:04:41,690 --> 00:04:42,860
This guy...

71
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:44,110
There it is!

72
00:04:44,910 --> 00:04:46,700
Good, it's in a case!

73
00:04:46,700 --> 00:04:49,080
I was worried
it might just be loose in there!

74
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:50,660
Okay! Let's hurry back!

75
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:55,290
Although, that pacifier seems to 
come with a lot of baggage.

76
00:04:55,290 --> 00:04:55,920
Huh?

77
00:04:56,250 --> 00:04:57,750
Did he tell you about it?

78
00:04:57,750 --> 00:04:58,670
Yeah.

79
00:04:58,670 --> 00:05:00,760
I asked why he was 
sucking on that it.

80
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:02,170
That was really direct!

81
00:05:02,170 --> 00:05:04,760
I mean, it'd be weirder not to ask.

82
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:07,600
I guess because it calms me down.

83
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:09,470
But if you ask me why...

84
00:05:10,260 --> 00:05:15,520
my mother, who isn't around anymore,
gave me a pacifier with a kind smile.

85
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:18,310
That hazy memory is the only one I have.

86
00:05:19,020 --> 00:05:22,320
Maybe it has something to do with that.

87
00:05:22,780 --> 00:05:25,570
He might have a pretty heavy past.

88
00:05:25,570 --> 00:05:27,530
Why not do the lap pillow?

89
00:05:27,530 --> 00:05:30,030
I don't think a lap pillow has
anything to do with that.

90
00:05:30,540 --> 00:05:33,160
Okay, what's happening with the game?

91
00:05:35,250 --> 00:05:36,580
What the heck happened?

92
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:38,000
Oh! You're back!

93
00:05:38,460 --> 00:05:41,590
Shin's been on fire,
making one god-tier save after another...

94
00:05:41,590 --> 00:05:43,090
against Tenma's killer shots!

95
00:05:43,090 --> 00:05:45,380
That's not "on fire"!
He's getting massacred!

96
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:47,010
Intercept!

97
00:05:48,140 --> 00:05:50,300
This is bad! Noren, get this to him now!

98
00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:51,060
Huh?

99
00:05:51,060 --> 00:05:53,600
If he takes any more of that,
he's gonna die!

100
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:55,980
Wait, die? But how am I supposed to...

101
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:56,940
Throw it!

102
00:05:56,940 --> 00:05:58,900
You're probably the best athlete here!

103
00:05:59,270 --> 00:06:01,860
Oh, for crying out loud! What is this?

104
00:06:02,150 --> 00:06:05,110
Shin! New pacifier incoming!

105
00:06:05,110 --> 00:06:07,030
ANPAN

106
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:14,370
- Huh?
- What the...

107
00:06:17,370 --> 00:06:20,920
Sorry, but things won't go
the way they did before.

108
00:06:20,920 --> 00:06:23,710
I'm quite confident in my footwork, too.

109
00:06:23,710 --> 00:06:24,840
He stopped it!

110
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:27,010
Is he the same guy as five seconds ago?

111
00:06:27,010 --> 00:06:28,760
- Shin!
- Shin!

112
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:31,100
All right, let's go!

113
00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:32,720
The real match starts now!

114
00:06:32,720 --> 00:06:35,730
Somehow, you're the only one
who's going into battle mode.

115
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:39,560
- Go!
- You can do it!

116
00:06:46,030 --> 00:06:48,820
That feint's totally basic,
but he's just plain fast!

117
00:06:49,610 --> 00:06:50,820
Dammit!

118
00:06:57,830 --> 00:07:00,710
Changing speed in a split second?

119
00:07:01,130 --> 00:07:02,340
That's it!

120
00:07:02,340 --> 00:07:05,210
The pacifier freak
isn't the only reason Tenma can't score!

121
00:07:05,210 --> 00:07:08,930
This guy looks like a total amateur,
but what the hell is he really?

122
00:07:11,970 --> 00:07:13,180
Out of bounds!

123
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:15,640
Aw, so close!

124
00:07:15,930 --> 00:07:19,060
That was incredible! Are you getting
better and better as we go?

125
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:23,440
Well, sure, I do wanna beat Tenma.

126
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:26,070
But that aside...

127
00:07:26,650 --> 00:07:29,820
Playing sports again after so long
is a ton of fun.

128
00:07:29,820 --> 00:07:32,370
Yeah! Wait, after how long?

129
00:07:32,370 --> 00:07:34,280
<i>That sounded too much
like an adult, Boss.</i>

130
00:07:34,580 --> 00:07:38,290
There's still tension, but it's nice
that nobody's trying to kill me.

131
00:07:38,290 --> 00:07:41,040
Trial and error and 
responding to the challenges...

132
00:07:41,330 --> 00:07:42,540
is kind of exciting.

133
00:07:47,510 --> 00:07:48,760
Hey, Tenma...

134
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:49,380
PEDESTRIAN TRAFFIC ONLY

135
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:50,170
Hm?

136
00:07:50,170 --> 00:07:53,510
The way you keep singling out Ogami...

137
00:07:54,510 --> 00:07:57,390
Is it because, deep down,
you're looking for a rival?

138
00:07:57,720 --> 00:07:58,520
Huh?

139
00:07:58,520 --> 00:08:02,600
You were born with that athletic physique,
but you never slack off, either.

140
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:04,560
You're superior in every sport you play.

141
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:06,610
But you're alone at the top. Maybe that's why...

142
00:08:06,610 --> 00:08:09,190
you're itching for someone
who can face you as an equal.

143
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:10,990
Nah, not at all.

144
00:08:10,990 --> 00:08:11,950
Huh?

145
00:08:11,950 --> 00:08:13,950
I like totally destroying people.

146
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:16,580
If I could win 100-0, I would.

147
00:08:16,950 --> 00:08:20,080
Wow, I was totally wrong!

148
00:08:20,660 --> 00:08:25,710
I'm doing three sports because 
I love all three too much to pick one.

149
00:08:25,710 --> 00:08:28,500
And that whole "alone at the top"
thing you mentioned?

150
00:08:28,500 --> 00:08:29,920
That's actually what I want to be.

151
00:08:30,510 --> 00:08:33,090
Every sport has its legends, right?

152
00:08:33,090 --> 00:08:35,970
And no matter how good
today's players are...

153
00:08:35,970 --> 00:08:38,430
they always get compared to those guys.

154
00:08:38,430 --> 00:08:40,020
That pisses me off.

155
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:42,940
But what if I leave behind legends
in three different sports?

156
00:08:43,230 --> 00:08:45,440
And not some soft,
watered-down kind of "unique."

157
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:48,440
I'm gonna be so one of a kind,
nobody can ever deny it.

158
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:53,400
He's so far gone, it's almost refreshing.

159
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:56,450
If we weren't childhood friends,
I'd stop hanging out with him.

160
00:08:56,820 --> 00:09:00,490
So, yeah, I'm not really looking
for a rival or anything.

161
00:09:00,870 --> 00:09:03,870
But I do have frustrations
from being all alone up here.

162
00:09:03,870 --> 00:09:04,500
Huh?

163
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:06,880
Huh?

164
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:07,840
What the...

165
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:09,300
All right!

166
00:09:09,300 --> 00:09:10,670
Yeah! Nice!

167
00:09:10,670 --> 00:09:11,840
This is getting fun!

168
00:09:14,010 --> 00:09:15,640
I said I like destroying people,

169
00:09:15,640 --> 00:09:17,800
but it's not like
I'm into kicking corpses, you know.

170
00:09:18,300 --> 00:09:20,310
It's just so hard to find...

171
00:09:20,640 --> 00:09:24,060
a toy I can play with at full strength
without breaking it.

172
00:09:24,810 --> 00:09:26,190
All righty!

173
00:09:26,190 --> 00:09:28,270
Time to get serious!

174
00:09:29,770 --> 00:09:31,530
He's not bluffing.

175
00:09:31,530 --> 00:09:35,280
I don't think I've ever heard someone say
a clichÃ© like that with a straight face.

176
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:43,410
People get this wrong all the time,
but when Tenma doesn't go all out...

177
00:09:43,410 --> 00:09:45,040
it's not exactly him playing around.

178
00:09:46,250 --> 00:09:49,840
All he ever thinks about
is improving himself.

179
00:09:49,840 --> 00:09:54,050
And to do that, he never actually
takes it easy on anyone.

180
00:09:54,380 --> 00:09:58,720
But if he overwhelms them too hard
and they give up, that's a problem for him.

181
00:09:58,720 --> 00:10:01,850
So, depending on the opponent,
he limits the kinds of plays he uses,

182
00:10:01,850 --> 00:10:03,600
or the area he's allowed to move in.

183
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:07,060
Basically, it's a self-improvement
challenge run.

184
00:10:07,690 --> 00:10:09,060
You should be proud.

185
00:10:09,650 --> 00:10:14,070
Tenma almost never takes
his shackles off in any sport.

186
00:10:22,450 --> 00:10:25,960
He's only dribbling!
But it's like trying to stop a boulder!

187
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:28,870
Hah!

188
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:31,710
Wha...

189
00:10:31,710 --> 00:10:33,380
Wha... So fast!

190
00:10:48,690 --> 00:10:49,980
Tenma scores!

191
00:10:49,980 --> 00:10:51,480
That's our superman!

192
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:54,360
No question about it!
A jaw-dropping three-man breakaway!

193
00:10:56,070 --> 00:10:57,900
And that's the end of the first half!

194
00:10:57,900 --> 00:11:00,570
Tenma's team heads into halftime
with a one-point lead!

195
00:11:01,120 --> 00:11:03,490
That was insane.

196
00:11:03,490 --> 00:11:06,660
I have to admit, even though we're
on Oga's side, that got us hyped, too!

197
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:09,830
Getting the crowd this fired up
with one play?

198
00:11:09,830 --> 00:11:11,960
That's pure superstar energy!

199
00:11:13,380 --> 00:11:14,960
Even three-on-one isn't enough.

200
00:11:15,590 --> 00:11:16,960
What are they supposed to do?

201
00:11:17,970 --> 00:11:20,010
Would you let me take them by myself?

202
00:11:20,010 --> 00:11:20,680
Huh?

203
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:22,470
Do you have some kind of plan?

204
00:11:22,470 --> 00:11:23,510
Nope.

205
00:11:23,510 --> 00:11:24,310
What?

206
00:11:24,310 --> 00:11:27,730
Well, I'm the one who picked this fight
in the first place.

207
00:11:27,730 --> 00:11:29,270
But never mind that.

208
00:11:30,310 --> 00:11:32,770
Anyway, just let me do this. Please.

209
00:11:35,570 --> 00:11:37,440
- Go!
- The second half is underway!

210
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:39,820
Does the home ec team have
any way to turn this around?

211
00:11:40,530 --> 00:11:41,240
Wait!

212
00:11:41,610 --> 00:11:42,990
Man-on-man?

213
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:45,200
You seriously think you can beat me?

214
00:11:45,580 --> 00:11:47,410
I'm taking point number two!

215
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:52,460
I can't shake him!

216
00:11:52,460 --> 00:11:53,500
Why not?

217
00:11:53,790 --> 00:11:55,420
What the hell is going on?

218
00:11:55,420 --> 00:11:59,630
Even if he's got freakish athletic ability, 
how can he keep up?

219
00:11:59,920 --> 00:12:01,340
Is it just me...

220
00:12:01,340 --> 00:12:03,590
or does Ogami look like he's...

221
00:12:04,100 --> 00:12:05,300
having fun?

222
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:09,770
It's not like I've got some chance
of winning, or some big plan.

223
00:12:09,770 --> 00:12:10,810
It's just...

224
00:12:10,810 --> 00:12:13,190
back when I was really a kid,
I hated losing.

225
00:12:13,560 --> 00:12:17,570
No matter how stupid the contest was,
I'd take it seriously.

226
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:19,780
But the more I grew up...

227
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:22,700
the less I got fired up about anything.

228
00:12:22,990 --> 00:12:26,450
At work, all that matters
is producing reliable results.

229
00:12:26,450 --> 00:12:29,790
But the more accomplishments
and years I stacked up,

230
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:32,670
somehow, life just kept
getting duller and duller.

231
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:36,000
I just remembered how I felt back then.

232
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:39,460
That feeling of playing my hardest and 
going head-to-head is damn great!

233
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:40,970
Thanks!

234
00:12:40,970 --> 00:12:43,470
Because of you,
I'm having a blast right now!

235
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:46,720
What are you, an old man?

236
00:12:46,720 --> 00:12:47,470
Crap!

237
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:49,970
But yeah, I agree.

238
00:12:49,970 --> 00:12:52,230
This is what a match oughta be!

239
00:12:52,230 --> 00:12:53,480
And in the end...

240
00:12:53,770 --> 00:12:54,690
I'm gonna win!

241
00:12:56,940 --> 00:12:58,400
This is one hell of a back-and-forth!

242
00:12:58,400 --> 00:13:00,190
- Go!
- Neither one's giving an inch!

243
00:13:02,490 --> 00:13:06,160
Just a minute ago,
he could barely keep up!

244
00:13:06,490 --> 00:13:09,080
There's no way Tenma's losing
in raw physical ability!

245
00:13:09,080 --> 00:13:10,950
Is he predicting Tenma's moves? No...

246
00:13:11,250 --> 00:13:13,250
He's getting a feel for his rhythm.

247
00:13:13,250 --> 00:13:16,670
Whether it's an official sport
or an underworld fight to the death,

248
00:13:16,670 --> 00:13:18,960
one-on-one, the fundamentals are the same.

249
00:13:18,960 --> 00:13:22,340
You identify the exact moment
your opponent will move and match them.

250
00:13:30,430 --> 00:13:31,810
It's a straight-up kicking clash!

251
00:13:31,810 --> 00:13:33,810
I swear I'm gonna win!

252
00:13:35,060 --> 00:13:36,690
They're even on sheer willpower?

253
00:13:37,150 --> 00:13:38,940
No, we are not even!

254
00:13:39,270 --> 00:13:41,820
I'm still holding one hell
of a grudge, you little punk!

255
00:13:43,400 --> 00:13:45,400
Don't look down on the home ec club.

256
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:47,200
Take a good, hard look
at yourself and do better!

257
00:13:47,820 --> 00:13:50,950
Don't do it because it's convenient
for you or whatever.

258
00:13:50,950 --> 00:13:53,660
Do it out of gratitude for the person
who made food for you!

259
00:13:55,500 --> 00:13:57,630
When someone makes you rice balls...

260
00:13:58,130 --> 00:14:00,710
how about giving them a thank you!

261
00:14:10,510 --> 00:14:13,390
It's in! Goal!

262
00:14:13,390 --> 00:14:14,390
It can't be!

263
00:14:14,390 --> 00:14:15,390
He scored!

264
00:14:15,390 --> 00:14:18,270
The home ec team comes out of nowhere
with the equalizer!

265
00:14:18,770 --> 00:14:19,900
- Yeah!
- We did it!

266
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:22,110
All right!

267
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:32,410
Man, what happened to you?
You actually lost a clash!

268
00:14:32,410 --> 00:14:33,740
Come on! We're getting
that point back!

269
00:14:43,750 --> 00:14:44,380
Hey...

270
00:14:52,760 --> 00:14:54,350
I give up.

271
00:14:54,640 --> 00:14:56,480
I can't keep going after that.

272
00:14:56,980 --> 00:14:58,350
I forfeit.

273
00:14:58,350 --> 00:14:59,690
This is my loss.

274
00:15:00,350 --> 00:15:01,020
Huh?

275
00:15:02,520 --> 00:15:04,070
What?

276
00:15:04,070 --> 00:15:06,070
What did he just say? He's giving up?

277
00:15:06,070 --> 00:15:07,030
That's it?

278
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:09,410
Give up? Why now?

279
00:15:09,410 --> 00:15:11,620
You're really fine after that?

280
00:15:11,620 --> 00:15:13,950
It's a shock for me, too.

281
00:15:14,950 --> 00:15:17,330
I hurt myself in that clash just now.

282
00:15:17,330 --> 00:15:20,040
If I keep pushing like that, it'll affect
the sports I'm serious about.

283
00:15:21,080 --> 00:15:23,170
I'm not looking down
on this game or anything.

284
00:15:23,170 --> 00:15:26,920
I only take stupid risks for the
sports I'm actually betting my future on.

285
00:15:26,920 --> 00:15:28,920
I hate to admin it, but I can't continue.

286
00:15:29,430 --> 00:15:30,380
Huh?

287
00:15:30,380 --> 00:15:31,430
We won?

288
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:34,100
Game set!

289
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:36,020
For real?

290
00:15:36,020 --> 00:15:37,600
Tenma lost?

291
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:40,060
Boo!

292
00:15:40,480 --> 00:15:43,860
Yeah, well, with an ending like that,
I can't blame 'em.

293
00:15:44,270 --> 00:15:45,650
Fair enough.

294
00:15:45,650 --> 00:15:47,280
I'll take the booing.

295
00:15:47,610 --> 00:15:48,860
More importantly, Ryohei...

296
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:50,990
can I lean on you?

297
00:15:50,990 --> 00:15:52,700
Walking's harder than I thought.

298
00:15:52,700 --> 00:15:55,740
What? Dude, you're huge and heavy!

299
00:15:56,290 --> 00:15:57,540
I know.

300
00:15:59,040 --> 00:15:59,960
Hey...

301
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:02,330
Is there tape in the first-aid kit?

302
00:16:02,330 --> 00:16:03,540
Well... yeah.

303
00:16:08,210 --> 00:16:09,720
Give me your foot.

304
00:16:09,720 --> 00:16:13,970
This isn't exactly my specialty,
but it'll be better than nothing.

305
00:16:13,970 --> 00:16:14,600
Probably.

306
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:19,270
The home ec club's president...

307
00:16:19,270 --> 00:16:22,100
Shiraishi. Chisato Shiraishi.

308
00:16:22,100 --> 00:16:23,850
Now the sock, too.

309
00:16:25,110 --> 00:16:26,230
Why?

310
00:16:26,570 --> 00:16:29,570
I still haven't apologized
like I promised.

311
00:16:30,110 --> 00:16:32,280
And besides, I'm the enemy.

312
00:16:32,280 --> 00:16:34,870
What are you talking about?

313
00:16:34,870 --> 00:16:39,790
Jeez, do battle maniacs only see
the world as enemies or allies?

314
00:16:40,290 --> 00:16:44,580
Now, it's true that your comments
got under my skin.

315
00:16:44,580 --> 00:16:46,500
In fact, I was ready to personally...

316
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:49,340
But... that's a separate matter.

317
00:16:49,340 --> 00:16:51,630
When someone's in trouble,
you help them.

318
00:16:51,630 --> 00:16:53,550
That's all there is to it.

319
00:16:54,430 --> 00:16:55,640
There. Done.

320
00:16:59,060 --> 00:17:01,980
That's the kind of club we are.

321
00:17:02,390 --> 00:17:07,900
That said, the fact that you have a clear
dream you're willing to put first...

322
00:17:08,270 --> 00:17:11,820
even if it means
getting booed in the moment...

323
00:17:12,150 --> 00:17:14,860
That's worthy of respect.

324
00:17:14,860 --> 00:17:16,530
I borrowed some crutches!

325
00:17:16,530 --> 00:17:17,200
Need these?

326
00:17:22,540 --> 00:17:24,330
Everyone in the home ec club...

327
00:17:24,330 --> 00:17:28,420
I'm not saying this because I promised to,
but because I truly mean it.

328
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:31,960
I'm sorry for making fun of you!

329
00:17:32,340 --> 00:17:34,630
The rice balls you brought were delicious!

330
00:17:34,630 --> 00:17:36,470
Thank you very much!

331
00:17:37,090 --> 00:17:40,970
For better or worse, he is honest.

332
00:17:46,150 --> 00:17:47,150
Hey!

333
00:17:47,480 --> 00:17:48,480
Huh?

334
00:17:48,480 --> 00:17:50,020
Ryo's with you, too?

335
00:17:50,020 --> 00:17:53,530
Yeah, I had a book I forgot to give Ogami.

336
00:17:53,900 --> 00:17:55,950
He should be here soon.

337
00:17:55,950 --> 00:17:57,070
Hey...

338
00:17:57,070 --> 00:17:58,070
Oh, Ogamiâ

339
00:17:58,870 --> 00:18:01,120
Ogami?

340
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:02,580
What happened to you?

341
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:07,830
Well, after all that, people
started recruiting me like crazy.

342
00:18:08,130 --> 00:18:11,040
I mean, you were pretty amazing out there.

343
00:18:11,040 --> 00:18:13,760
Like, not normal amazing.

344
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:18,340
That was a fluke! You know,
some kind of freak adrenaline rush!

345
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:20,220
<i>What are you gonna do?</i>

346
00:18:20,220 --> 00:18:22,850
<i>I told you that you'd end up
drawing a ton of attention!</i>

347
00:18:22,850 --> 00:18:24,020
What do I do?

348
00:18:24,020 --> 00:18:25,060
Hello!

349
00:18:27,350 --> 00:18:28,230
Huh?

350
00:18:28,230 --> 00:18:29,060
Why?

351
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:31,190
Tenma Tendo?

352
00:18:31,190 --> 00:18:34,570
Hey, don't look at me
like I'm some kind of ghost.

353
00:18:35,030 --> 00:18:38,070
Don't tell me you're here
to join the home ec club, too!

354
00:18:38,070 --> 00:18:39,490
No, I'm not.

355
00:18:39,820 --> 00:18:42,160
Also, why are you always 
sucking on that thing?

356
00:18:43,040 --> 00:18:45,160
There's something I have to do.

357
00:18:45,160 --> 00:18:46,000
Huh?

358
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,170
Well, more like something I want to say.

359
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:49,830
To you, Chisato.

360
00:18:54,300 --> 00:18:55,760
I've fallen for you.

361
00:18:56,090 --> 00:18:58,010
Please go out with me.

362
00:19:01,760 --> 00:19:02,510
Huh?

363
00:19:02,970 --> 00:19:04,770
What?

364
00:19:05,220 --> 00:19:07,810
I'm the best when it comes to sports...

365
00:19:07,810 --> 00:19:10,400
but outside of that,
I didn't understand anything.

366
00:19:10,810 --> 00:19:12,980
You made me realize that, Chisato...

367
00:19:13,440 --> 00:19:14,780
and now...

368
00:19:14,780 --> 00:19:16,780
I want to be with you forever!

369
00:19:17,030 --> 00:19:18,820
Wait... Huh?

370
00:19:18,820 --> 00:19:20,280
Hold on!

371
00:19:20,280 --> 00:19:21,740
This sort of thing is...

372
00:19:21,740 --> 00:19:24,030
I'm not used to it, or rather... why?

373
00:19:24,030 --> 00:19:28,460
I'm bad at this, but more like... 
how brutally direct is your approach to life?

374
00:19:30,790 --> 00:19:31,500
Master?

375
00:19:31,750 --> 00:19:33,920
What the hell do you think you're doing...

376
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:36,300
hitting on my precious big sister
out of nowhere?

377
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:37,510
I'll freaking kill you!

378
00:19:37,510 --> 00:19:39,800
Wait! Are you one of those
loves-his-big-sister-way-too-much guys?

379
00:19:40,180 --> 00:19:45,220
I don't care if you're a Unicorn
or popcorn, I'll grind you into meat!

380
00:19:45,220 --> 00:19:46,520
Calm down, Master!

381
00:19:46,890 --> 00:19:48,810
Tenma! Just get outside for now!

382
00:19:48,810 --> 00:19:49,430
Huh?

383
00:19:49,430 --> 00:19:50,270
Just do it!

384
00:19:50,270 --> 00:19:52,690
Master's already
in Thunderclap and Flash stance!

385
00:19:55,480 --> 00:19:57,900
Man, give me a break!

386
00:19:57,900 --> 00:20:00,820
What the hell were you thinking,
making a joke like that?

387
00:20:01,110 --> 00:20:02,990
It wasn't a joke. I'm serious.

388
00:20:02,990 --> 00:20:05,120
First Shin and now this guy...
What is with these people?

389
00:20:05,620 --> 00:20:09,120
Ever since that match, every sports club
 in the school has been chasing after me,

390
00:20:09,120 --> 00:20:11,500
I can't focus on my school life!

391
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:15,130
I just want to study quietly
without standing out!

392
00:20:15,460 --> 00:20:16,880
Without standing out?

393
00:20:16,880 --> 00:20:18,340
Quietly?

394
00:20:18,340 --> 00:20:19,590
You want to study?

395
00:20:19,590 --> 00:20:22,760
Right, you're the kind of guy
who wants to stand out, wants to excel...

396
00:20:22,760 --> 00:20:23,680
and doesn't want to study.

397
00:20:24,050 --> 00:20:25,850
That's impossible.

398
00:20:25,850 --> 00:20:27,430
You already stand out.

399
00:20:28,430 --> 00:20:32,640
I don't know what you're hiding,
but it's all gonna come out eventually.

400
00:20:32,640 --> 00:20:34,650
You're the least normal person here.

401
00:20:35,360 --> 00:20:40,150
An amateur doesn't beat me in a clash
by fluke or sheer guts alone.

402
00:20:40,530 --> 00:20:43,910
I've never seen anyone like you
at the top of any sport.

403
00:20:49,080 --> 00:20:50,750
Yeah, you're probably right.

404
00:20:50,750 --> 00:20:55,130
Even without all this,
it might only be a matter of time.

405
00:20:55,130 --> 00:20:57,540
But even so...

406
00:20:57,840 --> 00:21:03,430
I wouldn't trade this peaceful 
school life for anything.

407
00:21:03,430 --> 00:21:05,260
It's irreplaceable.

408
00:21:05,760 --> 00:21:06,550
So...

409
00:21:06,930 --> 00:21:10,060
I want to keep it going
for as long as I possibly can.

410
00:22:43,530 --> 00:22:46,860
After that, maybe as an apology to me...

411
00:22:46,860 --> 00:22:49,530
he pulled a little string for my sake.

412
00:22:49,530 --> 00:22:50,160
TENMA TENDO, VIRAL SUPER MIDDLE SCHOOLER,
BEGINS A LONG-TERM RECUPERATION

413
00:22:50,160 --> 00:22:51,950
Word got leaked that 
Tenma Tendo was injured...

414
00:22:51,950 --> 00:22:52,580
LONG-TERM RECUPERATION?
HIS INJURY MIGHT BE THE CAUSE?

415
00:22:52,580 --> 00:22:55,870
...and the sports magazines and news sites
were suddenly all over it.

416
00:22:55,870 --> 00:22:56,500
TENMA TENDO BEGINS
LONG-TERM RECUPERATION

417
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:57,120
YOUNG PRODIGY TENMA TENDO
BATTLING AN INJURY SINCE SPRING

418
00:22:57,120 --> 00:22:59,120
Of course, that wasn't actually true.

419
00:22:59,620 --> 00:23:01,250
The story he wanted to spread was...

420
00:23:01,250 --> 00:23:03,550
"The only reason
Juzo Ogami won"

421
00:23:03,550 --> 00:23:08,130
"was because Tenma was in nearly
the worst condition of his life."

422
00:23:08,470 --> 00:23:11,090
That took my reputation back down a peg,
relatively speaking.

423
00:23:11,090 --> 00:23:12,930
The sports club recruiting frenzy...

424
00:23:12,930 --> 00:23:15,470
and all the noise around me
gradually died down.

425
00:23:16,310 --> 00:23:17,350
Incidentally...

426
00:23:17,350 --> 00:23:21,400
When I asked him if that meant he'd be
sitting out all the summer tournaments...

427
00:23:21,940 --> 00:23:25,820
I'll just say I got healed up and 
make a miracle comeback!

428
00:23:25,820 --> 00:23:26,780
So, there you go.

429
00:23:29,200 --> 00:23:31,240
Worked out great, huh, Boss?

430
00:23:31,240 --> 00:23:34,830
Man, that was close.
I managed to cover it up somehow.

431
00:23:34,830 --> 00:23:35,790
Right?

